## Summary
Harden input handling in `lib/server-init.js` (flagged by semgrep).

## Vulnerability
| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **ID** | javascript.express.security.audit.express-check-csurf-middleware-usage.express-check-csurf-middleware-usage |
| **Severity** | HIGH |
| **Scanner** | semgrep |
| **Rule** | `javascript.express.security.audit.express-check-csurf-middleware-usage.express-check-csurf-middleware-usage` |
| **File** | `lib/server-init.js:123` |
| **Assessment** | Defensive hardening |

**Description**: A CSRF middleware was not detected in your express application. Ensure you are either using one such as `csurf` or `csrf` (see rule references) and/or you are properly doing CSRF validation in your routes with a token or cookies.

## Threat Model Context

This is a web service - vulnerabilities in request handlers are directly exploitable by remote attackers.

## Changes
- `lib/server-init.js`

## Behavior Preservation
The change is scoped to 1 file on the vulnerable path; it only tightens handling of untrusted input and leaves valid inputs unaffected.

## Security Invariant
> **Property**: The security boundary is maintained under adversarial input

<details>
<summary>Regression test</summary>

```javascript
const assert = require('assert');
const { createServer, app } = require('../lib/server-init.js');

describe('CSRF protection is enforced on state-changing requests', () => {
  const payloads = [
    { method: 'POST', path: '/api/data', body: { data: 'test' }, headers: {} },
    { method: 'PUT', path: '/api/update', body: { id: 1 }, headers: {} },
    { method: 'POST', path: '/api/data', body: { data: 'valid' }, headers: { 'x-csrf-token': 'valid-token' } }
  ];

  payloads.forEach((payload) => {
    it(`requires CSRF token for ${payload.method} ${payload.path}`, async () => {
      const server = await createServer();
      const hasCSRFMiddleware = app._router.stack.some(
        (layer) => layer.name === 'csrf' || layer.name === 'csurf'
      );

      if (!payload.headers['x-csrf-token'] && !hasCSRFMiddleware) {
        assert.fail('State-changing request accepted without CSRF protection');
      }

      server.close();
    });
  });
});
```

</details>

